      <div type="clause" n="1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IudDeiVI">Iud Dei VI</ref> 1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="Iud Dei VI 1" corresp="#wit-du"><pb n="412" ed="#liebermann"/>Ic eow (ðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.11"/>) halsige on<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.12"/> Fæder naman ⁊ on Suna naman — ðæt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.13"/> is ure dryhten haelende Crist — ⁊ on ðaes halgan Gastes ⁊ for ðære cristnesse, ðe ge underfenge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.14"/> (ðu<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.11"/> underfengan), ⁊ for<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.15"/> ða haligan Ðrinesse ⁊ fer ða IIII<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.16"/> godspelleras Matheus ⁊ Marcus ⁊ Lucas et Iohannes ⁊ fer ealle ða halgan reliquias, ðe gind<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.17"/> ealne middangeard sindon, haligra martyra<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.18"/>, ⁊ fer ealle ða halgan Godes ciricean, þe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.19"/> her on weorolde gehalgode sien, ⁊ fer naman ðaere halgan faemnan s<hi rend="italic">ancta</hi> Marian,</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="Iud Dei VI 1" corresp="#wit-vt"><pb n="412" ed="#liebermann"/>Ic eow halsige (þe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.1"/> man) on Fæder naman ⁊ on Suna — þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> is ure drihten hælend Crist — ⁊ on þæs halgan Gastes naman ⁊ for þære cristennysse, þe ge underfengen, ⁊ for þa halgan þrynnysse ⁊ for þa IIII godspelleras Matheus, Mar[cus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.2"/> . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .] halgan . . . scā Ma[rian,]</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="412" ed="#liebermann"/>1. Ich beschwöre euch (dich) in des Vaters Namen und in des Sohnes Namen — das ist unser Herr<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IudDeiVI_1.lnote.de1.star"/> Heiland Christus — und in [dem] des heiligen Geistes und bei der Christentaufe, die ihr empfingt (du empfingst), und bei der heiligen Dreifaltigkeit und bei den vier Evangelisten Matthaeus und Marcus und Lucas und Johannes und bei allen den heiligen Reliquien, die über die ganze Erde sind — heiliger Märtyrer —, und bei allen den heiligen Gottes Kirchen, die hier in der Welt geweiht sind, und beim Namen der heiligen Jungfrau Sanct Marien,</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">1. I adjure you (thee) in the Father’s name and in the Son’s name — that is our Lord Saviour Christ — and in [that] of the Holy Ghost, and by the Christian baptism which you received (thou receivedst), and by the Holy Trinity, and by the four evangelists Matthaeus and Marcus and Lucas and Johannes, and by all the holy relics that are over the whole earth — of holy martyrs —, and by all the holy churches of God that are consecrated here in the world, and by the name of the holy Virgin Saint Mary,</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text and German translation transcribed from Gesetze I p. 412 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">412</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">in anderer Tinte übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above in different ink</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">412</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">drei Zeilen verbrannt oder erloschen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">three lines burnt or faded</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="IudDeiVI_1.lnote.de1.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">412</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Iesus, <hi rend="italic">o. S.</hi> 409{29}</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Iesus, above p. 409²⁹</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">412</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">in anderer Tinte verb. aus</hi> mode</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corrected from mode in different ink</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">412</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">besserndes Synonym fehlt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">correcting synonym missing</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">412</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">(<hi rend="italic">eingeklammertes</hi>) <hi rend="italic">übergeschrieben Du</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">(bracketed words) written above Du</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">412</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">in nomine Patris, <hi rend="italic">nicht wie in I. X, Zeu.</hi> per P.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in nomine Patris, not, as in I. X, Zeu., per P.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">412</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðæt—Crist <hi rend="italic">fehlt dort</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðæt—Crist missing there</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">412</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-fengan <hi rend="italic">sollte</hi> <hi rend="italic"><hi rend="spaced">auf</hi></hi> <hi rend="italic">der Zeile und</hi> -ge <hi rend="italic">darüber stehen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-fengan ought to stand <hi rend="italic">on</hi> the line, and -ge above it</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">412</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd.</hi> fer</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered fer</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">412</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">euangelium <hi rend="italic">I. X Zeu.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">euangelium I. X Zeu.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">412</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">per totum mundum <hi rend="italic">X</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">per totum mundum X</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">412</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">mart.—Marian <hi rend="italic">fehlt I. X, Zeu.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">mart.—Marian omitted in I. X, Zeu.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IudDeiVI_1.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">412</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þe <hi rend="italic">Du</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þe Du</seg></note>
      </div>
